  "_note": "Quest definitions. Each player gets a deterministic pick of 3 daily quests (seeded by user and UTC date) and a chain of 5 weekly quests (seeded by user and ISO week), preferring distinct verbs. verb is a server event: shift_complete, perp_open, perp_close, prediction_place, alpha_call, paid_call (a funded call the payee accepted, counted for both sides, once per pair of players per 7 days), tip_send (Cash tip of at least 1000 cents, counted once per recipient per 7 days, never to someone who tipped the sender in the last 7 days), home_visit (someone else's home, once per home per 7 days, and not when the owner visited the visitor's home in the last 7 days). Progress comes only from server events, never from the client. reward.cashCents pays as ledger reason quest_reward; reward.seasonXp is recorded in season_xp. deepLink is the screen the client opens. The FE may reword titles; ids are stable. To add a quest, add it here: no code change. STARTER quests (pool 'starter') are not picked by date: each new account is given them once at first onboarding contact (never reseeded; accounts created before the onboarding migration get none). verb shift_start is a clock-in (Rekt Burger shift start or POST /shifts), trade_open a market buy or a perp open, chest_open the daily chest claim. q_starter_trade is only given while markets are live for the deployment (LIVE_PHASE >= 2).",
